WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.203
A plain timestamp stores a local date and time
without time-zone interpretation A

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:11.920
timestamptz represents an instant If data crosses
regions plain

00:00:11.933 --> 00:00:17.770
local timestamps can become ambiguous When the same
event must be understood

00:00:17.797 --> 00:00:21.928
consistently across systems timestamptz is usually
the safer model
